# Targets to delete from the destination on apply.
#
# Dropping a file from the source only makes chezmoi stop managing it; the copy
# already written to a machine stays exactly where it is. That is fine for most
# retired files and not fine for this one, so it is listed here explicitly.

# 10-autowatch.zsh hooked chpwd to `source` and then `eval` a .watchrc from
# whatever directory had just been entered, giving any cloned repository under
# ~/repositories arbitrary code execution on cd. direnv took over only its
# environment half, behind `direnv allow`; running a directory's scripts on cd
# waits on a replacement gated the same way (#7). Leaving the orphaned
# copy in place would keep it armed on every machine that ever applied it,
# since ~/.config/zsh/*.zsh is glob-sourced by .zshrc and would still pick it
# up. Safe to prune from this file once every machine has applied once.
.config/zsh/10-autowatch.zsh

# ~/.firefox-policies.json was only ever a staging copy: the 170-firefox-policies
# scripts read it and wrote it out to wherever that host's Firefox actually
# looks for policies.json. The document now lives in
# .chezmoitemplates/firefox-policies.json and is emitted inline by those
# scripts, so nothing reads this path any more -- but every machine that
# applied before the move still has it sitting in $HOME. Safe to prune from
# this file once every machine has applied once.
.firefox-policies.json

# ~/.vscode-extensions.txt was the VS Code extension list, read by the
# 160/800-install-vscode-ext scripts and nothing else. The list is now
# .chezmoidata/vscode.toml, rendered straight into those scripts, so the copy
# in $HOME is dead. Safe to prune from this file once every machine has
# applied once.
.vscode-extensions.txt

# xyz.regulad.xmrig.plist was a long-retired LaunchAgent for an xmrig miner
# under ~/xmrig. launchd loads every plist in ~/Library/LaunchAgents at login,
# so an orphaned copy would keep trying to start it on every Mac that ever
# applied it. Safe to prune from this file once every Mac has applied once.
Library/LaunchAgents/xyz.regulad.xmrig.plist

# osc52pty, the Go OSC 52 shim that 120-go-tooling installed into ~/go/bin,
# was replaced by terminal_polyfill (cargo-tools.toml) on 2026-11-25, and its
# fork is archived. On a Mac, Terminal.app's profile runs it as its startup
# command, set by hand (~/.bootstrap.sh): switch that to terminal_polyfill, or
# new Terminal.app windows fail to start. Safe to prune from this file once
# every machine has applied once.
go/bin/osc52pty

# Hook-only inputs moved to .chezmoidata/vim.toml and encrypted payloads in
# .chezmoitemplates/secrets. Imports now use private temporary files.
.coc-extensions.txt
.x509/client/dotfiles.p12
.gnupg/public_regulad@regulad.xyz.asc
.gnupg/secret_regulad@regulad.xyz.asc

# The hand-written SSH entries for hosts regulad/homelab now defines
# (docs/homelab-exports.md). 98-homelab sorts first, so its values win for the
# hosts it covers, but the old files would keep the aliases homelab dropped
# (the pct containers, the OCI instances, arawi) reachable with stale
# settings on every machine that ever applied them. Safe to prune from this
# file once every machine has applied once.
.ssh/config.d/99-cisco
.ssh/config.d/99-gonkputer-pve
.ssh/config.d/99-hardware
.ssh/config.d/99-matrix
.ssh/config.d/99-oracle-old
.ssh/config.d/99-oracle-vcn
